      "comment": "STORM SEASON (2) doesn't have to improve much to win this weaker race. Nailed late after taking control from the good draw to finish second over 1600m at this track. No excuses here and D-Day is looming. BURN THE SKY (4) stakes-placed mare fitter after two runs back. Much better performance when she stepped up to the mile to record a solid fourth over 1600m at this track. Tongue tie goes on and shapes as the main danger. KINGSTON CHARM (7) warmed up late second-up with a slashing fourth over 1600m in Midway BM72 grade at Randwick. Value contender. MIGHTY MYRTLE (8) is fitter for recent racing and looks close to a win after finishing a good second over 1600m at Canberra last time.",
